{"title":"2011 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(essentially_Solutions_1_and_2_but_cleaned_with_variables)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (essentially Solutions 1 and 2 but cleaned with variables)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(SIMPLE)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (SIMPLE)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A majority of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students in Ms. Demeanor's class bought pencils at the school bookstore. Each of these students bought the same number of pencils, and this number was greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The cost of a pencil in cents was greater than the number of pencils each student bought, and the total cost of all the pencils was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d153372047072d281d5911cdd25e0ce958c47208.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$17.71$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />. What was the cost of a pencil in cents?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/f/1ff6513ec0a378e15beb9180a0126d5b12b9d881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 7 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 11 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 17 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 23 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 77$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total cost of the pencils can be found by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11afa9812a0b0401f5b3bb5b4ff33cc61da905ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\text{students}\\cdot\\text{pencils purchased by each}\\cdot\\text{price of each pencil})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"427\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd30cd664ae5019ce20417381c20c397b741493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1771$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is the product of three sets of values, we can begin with prime factorization, since it gives some insight into the values: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1ce510cff6f0a78460a633e2a9cada48fa95603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7, 11, 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abd337e8b85dc471b3cb7c333dea9fd5d610a2f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(C)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"20\" /> has none of these factors, it can be eliminated immediately, leaving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565ab5e3715db52b9176b04dd9991b71f4e93a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313048c3149436615f6cd06b7f1bec83420d6a37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b4066cd24c53cd4053f840d210f974f46e1d913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(D)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02ad991c2821130f0d7e456d453252c19a320752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(E)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Beginning with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/9/369a8300604308f7966013dca9ebd68a479b6751.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A) 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" />, we see that the number of pencils purchased by each student must be either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. However, the problem states that the price of each pencil must exceed the number of pencils purchased, so we can eliminate this.\n</p><p>Continuing with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/9/8d90dd6af919c0b7f00d43250e29b37128057c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(B) 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"18\" />, we can conclude that the only case that fulfills the restrictions is that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students who each purchased <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> such pencils, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />. We can apply the same logic to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/a/02ad991c2821130f0d7e456d453252c19a320752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(E)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> as we applied to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565ab5e3715db52b9176b04dd9991b71f4e93a86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" /> if one wants to make doubly sure.\n</p><p>~PerseverePlayer (minor edits, changed some grammar, E can't be eliminated at first, fixed that)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know the total cost of the pencils can be found by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11afa9812a0b0401f5b3bb5b4ff33cc61da905ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\text{students}\\cdot\\text{pencils purchased by each}\\cdot\\text{price of each pencil})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"427\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Using prime factorization like in the solution above, we see that there is only one combination of three whole numbers whose product is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd30cd664ae5019ce20417381c20c397b741493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1771$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1ce510cff6f0a78460a633e2a9cada48fa95603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7, 11, 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" /> (without using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />). So we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/3/5c3139303e6338349fd81b636438fb038b6e2b80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7, 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must be the number of students, the number of pencils purchased by each student and the price of each pencil in cents.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must be the number of students, as it is the only number that makes up the majority of 30.\n</p><p>We pick the greater of the remaining numbers for the price of each pencil in cents, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2e33ab9a00e021af49e888212645d4667903c49.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{B}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p><p>-JinhoK\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28essentially_Solutions_1_and_2_but_cleaned_with_variables.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(essentially_Solutions_1_and_2_but_cleaned_with_variables)\">Solution 3 (essentially Solutions 1 and 2 but cleaned with variables)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (essentially Solutions 1 and 2 but cleaned with variables)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of students that bought pencils at the bookstore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be the cost of each pencil in cents, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> the number of pencils each student bought. Thus, we are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/1/201a2eef545643b50b07fed5c09e894bcced5c58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c.$\" width=\"11\" height=\"8\" /> \nSince a majority of the students in the class bought pencils at the bookstore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff52aab517ac9ae273821307e9a85fa6af12834.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s&gt;\\dfrac{30}2=15.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"104\" height=\"38\" /> (s&gt;15) We also know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ecccf1cda96ccb7ecaad549ad6a23e71373f7ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;n&gt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"83\" height=\"15\" /> Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a23a38f1cd865b992b01e935ce46d306555c9b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s\\cdot c\\cdot n=1771.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"121\" height=\"14\" /> We can factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/d/ecd30cd664ae5019ce20417381c20c397b741493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1771$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/0/cf04c5bbe089f4d4e74e82cb454d9e00018fb279.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\cdot11\\cdot23.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"79\" height=\"14\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e8535cad9f5eed2da662a47679d8c4a5777af0c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e6d8496bc3c7771c501fd2fa562d968cb20cc16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;n&gt;1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" /> none of them can be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bf27edd6ee0c25241392922eca9b9c9144f4d73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"17\" /> and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/6/4d6321a026ca8b41a8623b6448046afdcb9837ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c,n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/4/1e4cef427ae68b14c28f505097095888911b162b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7,11,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1b2497e7b125cd721bab4c6e2385f954fe35cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> in some order. We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/8/41841bd3240d9df1ff81771dc6b5bce1e57e9282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"17\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/9/7d9803b67b315db7dfce1c1ce717cfaaa8ec4d54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$23.$\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/41027b17ea3a2aed291bbe05129a3b36fe7f19b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c&gt;n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca87a6b24dce65aaa414a5db3f9608527f7f9af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59be54849236debd4606b3e8d22cf75384a09a96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/6/2b6ea7ddbd31d39c15a978734e70fd3a2638edf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=\\boxed{\\text{(B)}~11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"94\" height=\"30\" /> cents.\n~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6tlqpAcmbz4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6tlqpAcmbz4</a>\n~Shreyas S\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/E5UoNyFjSO0\">https://youtu.be/E5UoNyFjSO0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28SIMPLE.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(SIMPLE)\">Video Solution (SIMPLE)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (SIMPLE)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=biR0pgefTCs&amp;t=2s\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=biR0pgefTCs&amp;t=2s</a>\n</p><p>~piHard\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2011_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspa